==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|de}} {{term|porrée|lang=frm}}, which is from {{etyl|la|de}} {{term|porrum|lang=la}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈpɔʀeː]|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m||Porrees}}

# [[leek]]

====Usage notes====
''Porree'' is dominant in northern and central Germany, while ''Lauch'' is dominant in southern Germany and Switzerland; in Austria, neither is dominant.

